      "body": "Context: I am starting Mini-Project 2. I need to build a Python CLI script that organizes files in a folder. I need a clean Git history for the assignment submission.\n\nAction: \n1. Inside Intro_to_AI_mini_proj2, initialize a Git repository.\n2. Create a basic README.md with just the title \"# File Organizer CLI\" and save it.\n3. Create a blank Python file called organizer.py.\n4. Create a test directory called test_folder, and create three dummy files inside it: image_test.jpg, document_test.pdf, and video_test.mp4 (they can be empty text files, we just need the extensions).\n5. Make the first Git commit with the message \"Initial commit: setup project structure\".\n\nTone: Short, clear. Use bash commands for everything.\nCheckpoint: Show me the output of `git log --oneline` to confirm the first commit exists.",
