        "to_persona": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::OpenCodeAcpPersona"
      },
      "body": "Context: I am building a multi-agent pipeline for Mini-Project 2. We have a local Git repo in Intro_to_AI_mini_proj2. I need to create three sub-agents in .opencode/agent/ to handle different parts of the software development lifecycle.\n\nAction: Create the following three sub-agent .md files using the standard OpenCode frontmatter schema (description, mode: subagent, temperature, permission):\n\n1. .opencode/agent/script-writer.md\n   - Role: Writes Python code from scratch based on requirements.\n   - Pattern: \"understand, draft, verify\".\n   - Must output clean, PEP8-compliant Python code with comments.\n   - Temperature: 0.2, permission edit: allow, bash: deny.\n\n2. .opencode/agent/debugger.md\n   - Role: Fixes broken Python code when given a traceback error.\n   - Pattern: \"reproduce, diagnose, patch, verify\".\n   - Must explain the bug in plain English, then apply the fix using edit: allow.\n   - Temperature: 0.1, permission edit: allow, bash: deny.\n\n3. .opencode/agent/readme-writer.md\n   - Role: Generates Markdown README files for software projects.\n   - Pattern: \"gather, structure, document\".\n   - Must include: Title, Description, Installation/Requirements, and Usage (with terminal examples).\n   - Temperature: 0.4, permission edit: allow, bash: deny.\n\nTone: Match the standard OpenCode agent style \u2014 concise, structured, with numbered steps for the pattern.\nCheckpoint: Confirm the three file paths and show the frontmatter for each. Do NOT run them yet.",
