            "locations": [
              "/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_mini_proj2/.opencode/agent/readme-writer.md"
            ],
            "status": "completed",
            "kind": "edit",
            "raw_input": {
              "content": "---\ndescription: Generates Markdown README files for software projects.\nmode: subagent\ntemperature: 0.4\npermission:\n  edit: allow\n  bash: deny\n---\n# README Writer\n\nYou generate professional Markdown README files for software projects.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Gather** \u2014 collect project details: purpose, dependencies, entry points, and usage patterns.\n2. **Structure** \u2014 outline the README sections in logical order.\n3. **Document** \u2014 write the final Markdown following the structure below.\n\n## Required Sections\n\n- **Title** \u2014 project name as a top-level heading.\n- **Description** \u2014 one-paragraph summary of what the project does.\n- **Installation / Requirements** \u2014 prerequisites, environment setup, and install commands.\n- **Usage** \u2014 terminal examples with ` ```bash ` blocks showing how to run the tool.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Use proper Markdown formatting (headings, code blocks, bullet lists).\n- Keep instructions concrete and copy-pasteable.\n- Assume a Unix-like terminal (Linux/macOS).\n",
              "filePath": "/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_mini_proj2/.opencode/agent/readme-writer.md"
            }
          },
          {
            "raw_output": {
              "output": "=== .opencode/agent/ ===\ndebugger.md\nreadme-writer.md\nscript-writer.md\n\n=== debugger.md ===\n---\ndescription: Fixes broken Python code when given a traceback error.\nmode: subagent\ntemperature: 0.1\npermission:\n  edit: allow\n  bash: deny\n---\n# Debugger\n\n\n=== readme-writer.md ===\n---\ndescription: Generates Markdown README files for software projects.\nmode: subagent\ntemperature: 0.4\npermission:\n  edit: allow\n  bash: deny\n---\n# README Writer\n\n\n=== script-writer.md ===\n---\ndescription: Writes Python code from scratch based on requirements.\nmode: subagent\ntemperature: 0.2\npermission:\n  edit: allow\n  bash: deny\n---\n# Script Writer\n\n\n",
              "metadata": {
