              "prompt": "Write a Python script and save it to /home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_mini_proj2/organizer.py.\n\nExact technical specification:\n\n1. Import only: os, shutil, sys.\n2. Prompt the user: `path = input(\"Enter the path of the folder to organize: \")`\n3. Check if `os.path.exists(path)`. If False, print an error message and call `sys.exit(1)`.\n4. Define a dictionary called FILE_TYPES:\n   - \"Images\": [\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\", \".gif\"]\n   - \"Documents\": [\".pdf\", \".txt\", \".docx\"]\n   - \"Videos\": [\".mp4\", \".mov\", \".avi\"]\n5. Loop through all items in the folder.\n6. For each item, check if it is a file.\n7. Get the file extension.\n8. If the extension is in FILE_TYPES, do the following:\n   - Create the target folder (e.g., path/Images) if it doesn't exist.\n   - Use shutil.move() to move the file into that target folder.\n   - Print: `f\"Moved {filename} to {category}/\"`\n\nTone: Beginner-friendly. Add short comments explaining each step. Follow PEP 8 with type hints if applicable.\n\nUse the Write tool to save the file to /home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_mini_proj2/organizer.py. After writing, return the full code content in your response.",
