      "time": 1793011872.121638,
      "body": "Here's the problem:\n\n```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"organizer.py\", line 51, in <module>\n    main()\n  File \"organizer.py\", line 27, in main\n    for item in os.listdir(path):\nNotADirectoryError: [Errno 20] Not a directory: 'test_folder/image_test.jpg'\n```\n\n**What happened:** `os.path.exists()` returns `True` for files too, so the check on line 15 passes. Then `os.listdir()` blows up because you can't list the contents of a file.\n\n**Fix needed:** After the `exists` check, add an `os.path.isdir(path)` check to reject non-directory paths. Want me to patch this?",
