              "prompt": "Generate a README.md file for the project at /home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_mini_proj2 and save it to /home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_mini_proj2/README.md.\n\nThe project is a Python CLI script called \"File Organizer CLI\" that sorts files in a folder into subfolders (Images, Documents, Videos) based on their file extensions.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Title: \"# File Organizer CLI\"\n2. \"Description\" section explaining that it sorts files into folders by extension (currently supports Images: .jpg/.jpeg/.png/.gif, Documents: .pdf/.txt/.docx, Videos: .mp4/.mov/.avi)\n3. \"Requirements\" section: Python 3.x (no external packages needed, uses only standard library os, shutil, sys)\n4. \"Usage\" section showing the exact terminal command: `python organizer.py`, with an example terminal session showing the prompt and output (e.g., entering a folder path and seeing \"Moved X to Y/\" messages)\n5. Project structure section showing the key files (organizer.py, test_folder/)\n\nTone: Professional, clear, standard GitHub Markdown. Use proper headings, code blocks (bash), and bullet lists.\n\nUse the Write tool to save to /home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_mini_proj2/README.md. Return the full content in your response."
            },
            "raw_output": {
              "metadata": {
                "sessionId": "ses_e8817e917ffeEjOkHXWoOjYaZp",
