      "body": "Context: I need to push the multi-agent configuration and the chat history to GitHub to prove my AI workflow. However, I must NOT push the heavy .opencode/node_modules/ folder. \n\nAction: \n1. Create a .gitignore file in the root of the project with these lines:\n   .opencode/node_modules/\n   __pycache__/\n   *.pyc\n\n2. Force-add the agent definitions and the chat file:\n   git add -f .opencode/agent/\n   git add -f assistant.chat\n\n3. Commit them:\n   git commit -m \"docs: add multi-agent definitions and AI chat history for proof of workflow\"\n\nCheckpoint: Run `git status` and confirm that .opencode/node_modules/ is ignored. Then list the files you just successfully commited."
